lg:AT-ECG-s5-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "aab19ee867798a2f050ff02ca93f2c9b88c3f79596f45cabefc695032b2a62f0" ;
    lgo:text """(1) A service provider shall make at least the following information permanently, easily and directly accessible to users:
1. its name or company name;
2. the geographic address at which it is established;
3. details enabling users to contact it rapidly and directly, including its electronic mail address;
4. where applicable, the company register number and the company register court;
5. where the activity is subject to official supervision, the supervisory authority responsible for it;
6. for a service provider subject to trade or professional regulations, the chamber, professional association or similar body of which it is a member, the professional title and the Member State in which it was conferred, as well as a reference to the applicable trade or professional regulations and how to access them;
7. where applicable, the VAT identification number."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-ECG-s5-1-q1 .

lg:AT-ECG-s5-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "bc38f72afa5cfa2c6ff4f425c7136408d031c09b1018d25deb0cd15707aad107" ;
    lgo:text "(2) Where prices are stated in information-society services, they must be shown in such a way that an averagely attentive observer can easily read and attribute them. It must be clearly recognisable whether the prices are stated inclusive of value-added tax and all other duties and surcharges (gross prices) or not. It must also be stated whether shipping costs are included."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "SWE-2" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-ECG-s5-2-q1 .

lg:AT-FAGG-s4-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "15456e6a8c4abe283ac83ea2daf1a7a1ed329a7e95e088b5f80798f16146be41" ;
    lgo:text """(1) Before the consumer is bound by a contract or his contractual offer, the trader shall inform him in a clear and understandable manner of the following:
1. the main characteristics of the goods or services, to the extent appropriate to the means of communication and to the goods or services,
2. the name or business name of the trader, the address of his establishment, and his telephone number and email address by which the consumer can reach the trader quickly and contact him without particular difficulty,
3. where applicable
a) other online means of communication provided by the trader which ensure that the consumer can store any written correspondence with the trader, including the date and time of such correspondence, on a durable medium, and by which the consumer can reach the trader quickly and contact him without particular difficulty,
b) the business address of the trader differing from the address of his establishment, to which the consumer can address any complaint, and
c) the name or business name and the address of the establishment of the person on whose behalf the trader acts, and the business address of that person, if different, to which the consumer can address any complaint,
4. the total price of the goods or services including all taxes and charges, or, where the nature of the goods or services is such that the price cannot reasonably be calculated in advance, the manner in which the price is calculated, and, where applicable, all additional freight, delivery, postal or other charges or, where those charges cannot reasonably be calculated in advance, the fact that such additional charges may be payable,
4a. where applicable, the notice that the price was personalised on the basis of automated decision-making,
5. in the case of a contract of indeterminate duration or a subscription contract, the total costs incurred for each billing period and, where such contracts are charged at a fixed rate, the total monthly costs, or, where the total costs cannot reasonably be calculated in advance, the manner in which the price is calculated,
6. the costs of using the means of distance communication used to conclude the contract, where they are not charged at the basic rate,
7. the arrangements for payment, delivery and performance, including environmentally friendly delivery options where available, the period within which the trader undertakes to deliver the goods or perform the service, and any procedure provided for handling complaints by the trader,
8. where a right of withdrawal exists, the conditions, time limits and procedure for exercising that right, including provision of the model withdrawal form in Part B of Annex I and, where applicable, information on the existence and placement of the withdrawal function under § 13a,
9. where applicable, the consumer's obligation to bear the costs of returning the goods in the event of withdrawal from the contract under § 15 and, for distance contracts for goods which, by their nature, cannot normally be returned by post, the amount of the return costs,
10. where applicable, the consumer's obligation to pay a proportionate amount for services already performed in the event of withdrawal from the contract under § 16,
11. where applicable, the fact that there is no right of withdrawal under § 18, or the circumstances under which the consumer loses his right of withdrawal,
12. the existence of a legal guarantee of conformity for goods and its main elements, including its minimum duration of two years under Directive (EU) 2019/771 on certain aspects concerning contracts for the sale of goods, amending Regulation (EU) 2017/2394 and Directive 2009/22/EC and repealing Directive 1999/44/EC, OJ L 136 of 22.05.2019, p. 28, in a prominent manner using the harmonised notice in Annex II,
12a. where the producer grants the consumer a commercial guarantee of durability at no additional cost covering the entire goods for a period of more than two years and makes this information available to the trader, the information that such a guarantee applies to the goods, its duration, and a reference to the existence of the legal guarantee of conformity, in a prominent manner using the harmonised label in Annex III,
12b. the existence of the legal guarantee of conformity for digital content and digital services,
12c. where applicable, the existence and conditions of after-sales services and commercial guarantees,
12d. for goods with digital elements and for digital content and digital services, the minimum period, expressed as a period of time or by stating a date, during which the producer or provider supplies software updates, where the producer or provider makes this information available to the trader,
13. where applicable, relevant codes of conduct within the meaning of § 1(4) Z 4 UWG and how the consumer can obtain a copy of them,
14. where applicable, the duration of the contract or the conditions for terminating contracts of indeterminate duration or automatically renewed contracts,
15. where applicable, the minimum duration of the consumer's obligations under the contract,
16. where applicable, the trader's right to require the consumer to provide a deposit or other financial guarantees, and the conditions for them,
17. where applicable, the functionality of goods with digital elements (§ 2 Z 4 VGG) and of digital content and digital services, including applicable technical protection measures,
18. where applicable and relevant, the compatibility and interoperability of goods with digital elements and of digital content and digital services, insofar as the trader knows or can reasonably be expected to know this information,
19. where applicable, the possibility of access to an out-of-court complaint and redress mechanism to which the trader is subject, and the conditions for such access,
20. where applicable, the repairability score of the goods,
21. where item 20 does not apply and where the producer makes this information available to the trader, information on the availability, estimated cost and procedure for ordering spare parts necessary to maintain the conformity of the goods, on the availability of repair and maintenance instructions, and on repair restrictions."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-FAGG-s4-1-q1 .

