lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "934f0c8fdcfddd95c2757336b5e70a6ced50964478ae4775dd3ae1f874e53db1" ;
    lgo:text """(1) For the consumer, the following contractual provisions within the meaning of § 879 ABGB are in any event not binding, under which
1. the trader reserves an unreasonably long or insufficiently specific period during which he may accept or reject a contractual offer of the consumer or during which the consumer is bound to the contract;
2. particular conduct of the consumer is treated as the making or non-making of a declaration, unless the consumer is specifically advised at the beginning of the period provided for this purpose of the significance of his conduct and has a reasonable period to make an express declaration;
3. a declaration of the trader of legal significance for the consumer which has not reached him is treated as having reached him, unless it concerns the effectiveness of a declaration sent to the consumer's last notified address where the consumer has not notified the trader of a change of address;
4. a notification or declaration to be made by the consumer to the trader or to a third party must comply with a form stricter than written form or with particular requirements of receipt;
5. the trader is entitled on request to remuneration higher than that fixed at the conclusion of the contract, unless the contract also provides for a reduction in remuneration where the agreed conditions for a change in remuneration are met, the circumstances determining the change are described in the contract and are objectively justified, and the occurrence of the change does not depend on the trader's will.
6. the consumer's right under § 1052 ABGB to withhold his performance until the counter-performance is effected or secured is excluded or restricted where the trader does not perform in accordance with the contract or where performance is endangered by his poor financial circumstances of which the consumer neither knew nor ought to have known at the time of the conclusion of the contract, for example by making the right of retention conditional on the trader acknowledging defects in his performance;
7. a right of retention to which the consumer is entitled by law is excluded or restricted;
8. the consumer's right to discharge his liabilities by set-off is excluded or restricted in the event of the trader's insolvency, or counterclaims which are legally connected with the consumer's liability and which have been judicially established or acknowledged by the trader are excluded or restricted;
9. a duty of the trader to compensate for personal injury is excluded or restricted, or a duty of the trader to compensate for other damage is excluded or restricted where he or a person for whom he is responsible has caused the damage intentionally or by gross negligence;
10. the trader, or a body or person within his sphere of influence, is authorised to decide with binding effect on the consumer whether the services provided to the consumer by the trader conform to the agreement;
11. a burden of proof is imposed on the consumer which he does not bear by law;
12. the consumer's rights to an item taken over by the trader for processing lapse within an unreasonably short period;
13. the interest payable in the event of the consumer's default exceeds the rate of interest agreed for payment in accordance with the contract by more than five percentage points per year;
14. the right to invoke a mistake made by him, or the absence or lapse of the basis of the transaction, is excluded or restricted in advance, for example also by an agreement that statements of the trader do not concern the main subject matter or an essential characteristic of it (§ 871(1) ABGB);
15. after the occurrence of default he undertakes to pay collection or enforcement costs, unless those costs are separately and itemised in the agreement, or insofar as those costs were not necessary for the appropriate collection or enforcement of the claim."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-1-q1 .

lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "08a14972abf4dbbe4c3de4815293dd821aa467bd865aa141a9d063ba65cb2e38" ;
    lgo:text "(3) A contractual provision contained in general terms and conditions or standard contract forms is ineffective if it is worded unclearly or unintelligibly."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-3-q1 .

